.TH SCHOOLAPP 1 "2026-08-20" "schoolapp-watcher" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
schoolapp \- semester-first CLI for ENSAM SchoolApp: fetch, cache, watch, and serve your own results
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B schoolapp
.RI [ global-options ]
.RI [ command
.RI [ args ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B schoolapp
is one front-end over a shared library, a local state store, and a read-through
API. It never talks to the portal on your behalf without you asking: commands
are split into three kinds, and the split is the whole design.
.PP
.B Live
commands log into the SchoolApp portal with your credentials, fetch fresh
data, and persist it to the local store
.RI ( ~/.local/state/schoolapp
by default).
.B Read
commands never touch the network: they only display whatever the last
.B Live
fetch already cached, which is what makes them safe to run often, offline, or
from a script.
.B serve
exposes that same store over HTTP, read-through, for the plasmoid and Android
front-ends to poll instead of hitting the portal themselves.
.PP
.B s3
and
.B s4
are per-semester namespaces with their own
.BR list ", " table ", " details ", " calc ", and " watch
subcommands, since a student is usually working one semester at a time.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR --quiet ", " --no-banner " (" -q )
Silence the startup banner and log chrome; only real output remains on
stdout.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Path to a config TOML file. Default:
.IR ~/.schoolapp/config.toml .
.TP
.BI --env-file " PATH"
Load
.I KEY=VALUE
env vars from
.IR PATH .
If not given, the CLI looks for
.I .env
then
.I .env.example
in the current directory or project root; if only
.I .env.example
exists it is copied to
.I .env
(mode 600 where possible) so you have something to edit.
.SH LIVE COMMANDS (portal login)
.TP
.B doctor
Print effective runtime config and run optional health checks. Start here
when something looks wrong.
.TP
.B profile
Fetch the student profile
.RI ( /index ),
cache it, and display it.
.TP
.BI fetch-all " [--no-save]"
Fetch every per-student resource in one pass; persists to the store unless
.BR --no-save .
This is what most automation (a login-time watcher, a cron job) should call.
.TP
.BI export " [--pdf]"
Fetch everything and write a JSON archive, optionally bundling the document
PDFs.
.TP
.BI promo " CODE"
Reconstruct the whole promotion's grades for one element, anonymized.
.TP
.BI promo-sem " ..."
Reconstruct the whole promotion's semester moyennes, anonymized.
.TP
.BI promo-year " ..."
Reconstruct the whole promotion's année moyennes, anonymized.
.TP
.B documents list
List document descriptors from the store and whether each PDF is already
cached.
.TP
.B documents download
Download attestation / relevé PDFs, caching them into the store.
.SH READ COMMANDS (offline, from the store)
These never touch the network; they mirror exactly what
.B serve
would answer.
.TP
.B status
Per-resource freshness: what the API would serve right now, and how old it
is.
.TP
.B dashboard
The default when no command is given: who you are, latest results, store
freshness, recent changes.
.TP
.B changes
Change history: the same feed the email digests narrate.
.TP
.BI csv " RESOURCE " "[-o FILE] [--latest]"
Export marks, or NoteRAT/exam ranking stats, as CSV.
.I RESOURCE
is one of
.IR elements ", " grades ", " modules ", " semesters ", " years ", " courses ", " absences .
Writes to stdout unless
.B -o
is given;
.B --latest
restricts elements/grades to the latest académique year.
.TP
.BI explain " CODE " "[--json]"
Règlement walkthrough for one element: how SO/SR/decision are computed, with
the articles cited. See
.B RÈGLEMENT
below.
.TP
.B show
Display cached data from the store. Subcommands:
.IR all ", " profile ", " grades " (add " --modules " for module-level), " semesters ", " years ", " courses ", " absences .
.SH SERVER
.TP
.BI serve " [--host ADDR] [--port N] [--threads N] [--reload]"
Serve the read-through API over the same store the watcher writes. Reads
credentials/API key from whatever
.B --env-file
or
.B --config
already loaded, so
.B "schoolapp --env-file .env serve"
is the one-liner the plasmoid/Android app point at. Default bind
.IR 0.0.0.0:8787 ,
waitress with 4 threads;
.B --reload
swaps in Flask's dev server for autoreload during development.
.SH SEMESTERS
.B s3
and
.B s4
each provide:
.TP
.B list
List modules and elements for that semester.
.TP
.B table
Fetch and show a consolidated grade table (API3*/API4* elements).
.TP
.BI details " ELEMENT"
Detailed grade breakdown for one element.
.TP
.B calc
Run the interactive weighted calculator for that semester.
.TP
.B watch
Watch that semester's marks for changes, diffing snapshots.
.SH CATALOG
.TP
.B catalog crawl
Crawl the institution-wide (niveau × filière × semestre) curriculum catalog
into the store. Incremental, re-running merges rather than replaces.
.TP
.B catalog show
Show cached catalog modules, with element weights, for one
niveau/filière/semestre combination.
.SH RÈGLEMENT
.B explain
and the
.B s3 " / " s4 " " table
views apply the official ENSAM evaluation règlement (CE 2019-10-22 /
CU 2019-12-25): after a rattrapage, the element moyenne is
.IR "max(SO, max(0.3\(muCC + 0.7\(muRat, Rat))" " (Art. 7),"
and a module is validated per its own article-specified rule. Run
.B "schoolapp explain CODE"
to see the computation and the exact article applied to a given element.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Credentials and SMTP settings come from, in order of precedence: CLI flags,
.BR --env-file / --config ,
then the auto-loaded
.I .env
described under
.BR GLOBAL\ OPTIONS .
.PP
Env vars:
.IR SCHOOLAPP_EMAIL ", " SCHOOLAPP_PASSWORD ,
.IR SMTP_HOST ", " SMTP_PORT ", " SMTP_USERNAME ", " SMTP_PASSWORD ", " SMTP_FROM ", " SMTP_TO .
.PP
Config file
.RI ( ~/.schoolapp/config.toml ):
.RS
.nf
[schoolapp]
email = "you@example.com"
password = "secret"

[smtp]
host = "smtp.gmail.com"
port = 587
username = "you@gmail.com"
password = "app-password"
from = "you@gmail.com"
to = "you@gmail.com"
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/schoolapp
The local store: everything
.B Read
commands and
.B serve
answer from.
.TP
.I ~/.schoolapp/config.toml
Optional config file (credentials, SMTP).
.TP
.I .env " / " .env.example
Project-local env file, auto-loaded if
.B --env-file
is not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Log in once and populate the store:
.RS
.nf
schoolapp fetch-all
.fi
.RE
.PP
Everyday offline check, and one semester's table:
.RS
.nf
schoolapp
schoolapp s4 table
.fi
.RE
.PP
Understand why an element passed or didn't:
.RS
.nf
schoolapp explain API421
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export grades for a spreadsheet:
.RS
.nf
schoolapp csv grades -o grades.csv
.fi
.RE
.PP
Point the plasmoid/Android app at a local read-through API:
.RS
.nf
schoolapp --env-file .env serve
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR README.md ", " CLAUDE.md
in the project checkout.
